TreeSet in Java is a class that implements the Set interface and uses a tree for storage. It is part of the Java Collections Framework
   It provides a way to store unique elements in a sorted order.
   The TreeSet class is based on the Red-Black tree data structure, which allows for efficient insertion, deletion, and search operations.

 👉 Stores elements in sorted order
 👉 Uses a Red-Black Tree internally
 👉 Does not allow duplicates or null

Set → SortedSet → NavigableSet → TreeSet

A Red-Black Tree is a:
 Self-balancing Binary Search Tree (BST)
 Keeps height balanced
 Guarantees O(log n) operations

