Natural Ordering (Comparable)
    - TreeSet uses the natural ordering of elements (defined by the compareTo method of the Comparable interface) to sort the elements in the set.
    - If the elements do not implement the Comparable interface, a ClassCastException will be thrown at runtime when you try to add an element to the TreeSet.

TreeSet -> TreeMap -> Red-Black Tree
    - TreeSet uses a TreeMap internally to store its elements.
    - Each element in the TreeSet is stored as a key in the TreeMap, with a constant dummy value (often `Boolean.TRUE`) associated with it.
    - This allows the TreeSet to leverage the efficient sorting and lookup capabilities of the TreeMap while providing the unique element storage and set operations defined by the Set interface.

