TreeSet must implements Comparable for natural ordering or provide a Comparator for custom ordering

when implements Comparable it must override compareTo method
    - compareTo returns a negative integer, zero, or a positive integer as this object is less than, equal to, or greater than the specified object.

when using Comparator it must override compare method
    - compare returns a negative integer, zero, or a positive integer as the first argument is less than, equal to, or greater than the second.

@Override
    public int compareTo(TreeSetLearning o) {
        return 0; // 0 means it will consider all objects as equal and only one will be stored in the TreeSet
        return this.value - o.value; // for natural ordering based on value
        return 1; // this will allow all elements to be added to the TreeSet, but they will not be sorted in any specific order
    }
